    "description": "Hospital, level 3 of 3: L2 plus flourish 3. Needs scaffolding: 13 tall. Over budget: 1,654 blocks (L1 1,447) vs the infirmary's 285 (no hospital budget in the brief; under the landmark 1,800). The infirmary's tier-6 big brother, a two-storey cloister hospital round a 5 x 5 herb courtyard: stone brick ground storey, white plaster in a dark oak frame above with the red wool cross over the door, one spruce roof round the ring (dark oak hips and eaves) with a front gable and a kiln chimney. 14 beds, dispensary, healers' room, herb store, clay room (rebuilding fallen soldiers), a staircase; courtyard pool by the decoration step. L2 a covered entrance porch, red banners, brewing stands, cauldrons, candles, lanterns, carpets, courtyard herbs, planters, shutters, clay; L3 a front herb garden with lantern posts, corner banners, a herb strip on the left, a log pile, barrels. Not yet builder-tested: allium, azure_bluet, brewing_stand, candle, cauldron, clay, cornflower, fern, oxeye_daisy, red_wall_banner, sweet_berry_bush. Decoration step adds: lily_pad, potted_plant, water.",
    "changes": "QC v1: the red cross now reads on every level (red wool on a white wool field on the upper storey over the door, as the infirmary v4); the plain white banners are gone (red banners from L2). L1: two-tall outer windows with front shutters, poppy planters with trapdoor fronts and corner bushes, a proper 9-wide front gable with a plaster face and window, dark oak hips, valleys and verges on the spruce roof, a front yard with a path (the building moved back 2 rows). L2: a covered entrance porch with hanging lanterns and benches, two more planters with trapdoor fronts. L3: a front herb garden either side of the porch with lantern posts.",
    "parent": 1,
    "reviewedAt": "2026-10-10T09:16:21.515Z",
